From 83dad837152a846baee7fc70b3b8f070c44e36c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:28:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(repair): open the hosted pre-review CI fix route; refresh
 pre-review parks on a moved base (#153)

Generation 81 has R80 e48e7e110 as its rollback target. Generation 80 kept
the hosted pre-review CI fix route closed because R79 refused that cell, so
every red head no completed review binds parked `CI red before review;
awaiting a CI fix: ...` with no way out. That includes the refreshed head of
every reviewed record whose base moved (645, 646, 649, 1128, 583, 615, 617,
629 and 633 at the integration review). A park also almost always outlived
its base, and the exhausted park got no flake re-run.

Runtime (src/, takes effect when R81 is installed):
- HOSTED_PRE_REVIEW_CI_FIXES is true. In a hosted run the gate now gives a
  red, never-reviewed head the CI fix marker instead of parking it. The head
  may be a new candidate or a reviewed record's refreshed head. The matrix
  planner then admits the fix as a cell, charged in counters.retries. It is
  never a review round, at most 3 per record, and then the exhausted park.
  No new state shape, cell kind or stdout line is added.
- Only comments change in loop-ci-first.ts and matrix-planner.ts.

Launcher (ops/, may ship before the runtime and is correct under R80):
- Moved base: under a proven CI-first runtime (R80 included), a red or
  pending pre-review park whose base moved returns to `work` uncharged with
  no marker (`retry:<id>:grant=0:...:base-moved`). The runtime's freshness
  gate refreshes it deterministically, and its CI gate runs before any
  review. It needs a review round left by the ceiling's own count, because
  the runtime's ceiling gate would otherwise park it before the refresh. An
  open legacy final round is a CI fix's to arm. The unchanged-base condition
  now applies only to the any-runtime green rule.
- Exhausted park: the pre-review gate's exhausted park of a head no completed
  review binds gets the once-per-head re-run and the green rule. It never
  gets a fix or a moved-base refresh. The merge gate's exhausted park of a
  reviewed head belongs to delivery, so it keeps generation 80's terms.
- Fix rule: it re-admits an R80-written red park on its unchanged base
  through the CI fix marker, only under a fix runtime.
  HOSTED_AUTONOMY_CI_FIRST_FIX_RUNTIMES stays empty here; generation 81's
  pin commit lists R81 there and in the CI-first and CI-correction
  allowlists. ciFirstFixRuntimeProven counts a listed revision only at
  generation 81+, as a proven CI-first runtime with its own healthy proof. A
  test proves HOSTED_PRE_REVIEW_CI_FIXES true in every listed revision's tree.
- The misleading "the runtime's freshness gate owns it" test comment is
  fixed. The runtime skips blocked records.

Rollback to R80 (tests guarded on R80's source being present, since CI
checkouts are shallow):
- R80's consumer isolates every pre-review fix cell generation 81 plans as an
  authenticated runtime mismatch with the charge kept reserved. This covers a
  never-reviewed head, a reviewed record's refreshed head, and both legacy
  shapes. The two shapes no planner grants keep the generic refusal, so R80
  refuses nothing it already isolated.
- R80's parsers accept the planned plan and every snapshot written by the
  hosted gate, the planner and the retry pass.
- R80's own loop parks the CI fix marker precisely and uncharged.
- R80's own loop runs the launcher's moved-base return as one deterministic
  refresh with nothing charged. The red refreshed head parks; the green one
  gets exactly one review.

Live (read-only):
- At repair sequence 41064 (2026-10-17T20:18Z, R80 installed at generation
  80), two ai.ubq.fi records sit in the CI-red pre-review park.
- 1148 (PR 1149, never reviewed) is on 3650359812 while development is
  e25d09cd09. L80 never re-admits it; this launcher returns it under R80 at
  once for its uncharged refresh.
- 575 (legacy, final round armed by R80's correction, one round left) is on
  the tip. It waits for a base move (refresh), a green head (green rule), or
  a pinned R81 once its re-run settles (CI fix marker).
- At sequence 40627 (R79 installed) no record sat in these parks, and the
  launcher's plans were identical to L80's.

Tests: hosted-autonomy-ci-first, hosted-autonomy-legacy-round-gate,
hosted-autonomy-pre-review-pass (new, real retry pass under the exact R80),
matrix-pre-review-fix (new), matrix-ci-first-gen79 (R80 consumer cases),
ci-first-refresh-red, ci-first-gate, ci-first-rollback-gen79,
ci-first-rollback-gen80 (new). gen80 source and parser helpers added to
tests/host/gen77-runtime-source.ts and tests/state/gen77-contracts.ts.

